Rust pairing fixtures, read by internal/pairing/declared_test.go through the
real parser (repoindex.TestModules). Nothing here is compiled.

warp/     Paths and #[path] lines from the local Warp fork
          (~/PycharmProjects/warp, HEAD 325d4d4701b41feb272487e89a6cf02bfba9f194). Each source keeps
          its module declaration VERBATIM (the #[cfg(test)], #[path] and mod
          lines); every other line of the real file is elided. The test files
          are stubs: pairing reads their existence, never their contents.
layouts/  Constructed trees for the forms Warp does not use at those paths:
          rustc's default module file (mod.rs and non-mod.rs), a #[path] with
          ../ into a sibling directory, an inline module, a source with no
          test module, a #[path] that names a missing file, and one that
          escapes the repository.
